<title>ECUADOR: Ecuador bank liquidity down 0.33 percent.</title>
<headline>Ecuador bank liquidity down 0.33 percent.</headline>
<dateline>QUITO, Ecuador 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ecuador's Central Bank said Monday liquidity in the banking system fell 0.33 percent or 61 million sucres to 18.31 billion sucres ($4.18 billion) in the week to March 7.</p>
<p>At the end of February, bank liquidity was at 18.37 billion sucres.</p>
<p>Total liquidity in the banking sector stood at 16.99 billion sucres at the end of 1996, up 35.8 percent from a year earlier.</p>
<p>((--Gustavo Oviedo, Quito Newsroom, 5932 258433))</p>
